Status: Working legal projection, not yet an in-setting judgment.

LOCKED: Furui Tokyo has a legal system broadly similar to real Tokyo/Japan.

WORKING LEGAL CLASSIFICATION:

- Immediate hotel-area deaths are likely prosecuted as multiple intentional murders under conditional intent: James deliberately used an indiscriminate lethal effect in an occupied downtown hotel even if he did not desire civilian deaths.

- The larger earthquake, SPAA escalation, and Gate catastrophe are more plausibly prosecuted as grossly negligent or recklessly caused supernatural catastrophe unless expert testimony establishes that those consequences were reasonably foreseeable.

- Self-defense or emergency necessity is unlikely to justify the scale of force used unless the spirit beasts posed a genuinely comparable immediate threat.

- Confession, voluntary surrender, immediate rescue activity, Gate closure, cooperation with authorities, and prevention of one to two million additional deaths are extraordinary mitigation but do not erase the original crimes.

PROVISIONAL OUTCOME:

- Capital prosecution is appropriate.

- A trial court may impose death for multiple murders and catastrophic magical destruction.

- The recommended campaign outcome is commutation to life imprisonment under permanent magical-security restrictions because James’s continued supervised assistance may be essential to preventing further deaths.

- Possible conditions include no unsupervised High Magic, magical monitoring or sealing, mandatory disaster-response service, victim compensation, restrictions on dimensional travel, and state-supervised deployment.

LOCKED THEMATIC RESULT: James becomes both the convicted perpetrator of Furui Tokyo’s greatest disaster and one of the principal people who saved the city from complete destruction.
